I'm not surprised that some of you haven't heard of the OMELET.  It's
one of the most difficult things to get in the game.  The Amulet is just
one step on the way to getting the OMELET.  Some people foolishly 
sacrifice the Amulet to their god on level 0.  These people are content
to just become DEMI-gods.  

To becmoe a full God, get the Amulet of Yendor, wear it, and level teleport
to level -11.  (Normally you can't level teleport with the Amulet, but
when you're standing on your God's altar on level 0 you can).  Level
-11 is Heaven.  This is where you'll find "God's Kitchen".

(a)pply the Amulet, to heat the stove, and then place a cockatrice egg
on it (Oops -- did I forget to tell you to bring one?).  When the
egg cooks, eat it.  You must wait exactly 723 turns for it to be 
perfectly cooked.  Less and you'll turn to stone, more and it will
burn, and your god will spell the smoke, and appear and kill you.
(Although this means you lose, the messages are quite entertaining,
and I recommend you try doing it at least once).

Eat the Omelet, and you'll become a God, and will have one final battle
AGAINST your God to replace him/her as the new God of your alignment.
Then everyone playing on your system will see your name instead of the
old God.   I had a really tough time figuring all that out without
reading the source, but the reward was worth it.

Good Luck!
